      "id": 1,
      "text": "Benoni Dawson laid out Georgetown across Little Beaver Creek in 1793, after building a fortified log cabin there seven years earlier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/georgetown.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The River Hotel, built in 1802, still stands today as a private residence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/georgetown.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Georgetown thrived as a river town until railroads became the primary means of transport.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/georgetown.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Georgetown sits in Beaver County, western Pennsylvania, just north of the Ohio River and southwest of Pittsburgh.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.citydirectory.us/borough-georgetown-pennsylvania.html"
    },
    {
